course: dictionary
lesson: 1884
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right. In «Old coins and notes can stop being accepted in shops, but collectors may want rare ones», collectors are people who keep things they enjoy, because they want rare coins.
explain: In «Jesus ate with tax collectors and sinners», a collector is a person whose job is to collect money. The word before it, tax, is a clue. Compound phrases help too: stamp collector, ticket collector and rubbish collector each tell you what is collected.
explain: Ask two questions. Is this person keeping things for fun, or gathering something as their job? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A collector is a person who collects things of one kind as a hobby, such as stamps, coins, cards or shells.
fact: A collector can also be a person whose job is to collect money or things, such as a ticket collector or a rubbish collector.
fact: In science and technology, a collector is a part that gathers something, such as a solar collector that gathers heat from the sun.
fact: «Sanitation engineer» is a joking or puffed-up name for a rubbish collector, used in the US.
fact: Tip: when a word has several meanings, the words around it show you which one the writer means.
exercise: In «Sundarbans honey collectors once wore face masks on the backs of their heads», what are the collectors? | Shops that sell honey | People who keep stamps as a hobby | Parts that gather heat from the sun | *People whose job is to gather honey
exercise: Which phrase names a person who keeps things for fun? | tax collector | ticket collector | *stamp collector | rubbish collector
exercise: «Collectors may want rare ones.» What might collectors want? | *Rare coins | Bus tickets to check at the gate | Rubbish bins to empty | Heat from the sun
test: What does a ticket collector do? | Keeps stamps in a book at home | Sells honey in a shop | Gathers heat from the sun | *Checks and takes tickets at a gate
test: In science, what does a solar collector do? | Cleans the streets | Counts money in a bank | Collects stamps and coins | *Gathers heat from the sun
exam: Which sentence shows collector as a job? | *«The ticket collector checked everyone's tickets at the gate.» | «My friend is a keen stamp collector.» | «He is a proud coin collector.» | «She has a big shell collection on her shelf.»
